From eb13581a121aa37f7129f87e13c7c245d198de1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:27:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: settings as JSON (GET/PUT /api/v1/settings) for
 the web UI

The web UI's Config page needs the device settings as data instead of the
config terminal. /api/v1/settings returns them per section (acsi,
translated, shared, floppy, network, ikbd, other, hddimage), the same
settings as the Atari config screens. PUT /api/v1/settings/<section>
saves one section with the same checks, settings keys and reloads as that
screen's save function (onAcsiConfig_save, onTranslated_save, ...).

- Secrets are never returned: the shared drive password and the Wi-Fi key
  are reported as passwordSet / pskSet. Leaving them out of a PUT keeps
  them.
- PUT accepts only application/json, so a cross-site form post from
  another web page can't change settings without a CORS preflight.
- Text that ends up in config files is checked: no quotes, backslashes
  or control characters in the Wi-Fi name and key (written quoted into
  wpa_supplicant.conf), the shared drive fields and the NTP server;
  hostnames are letters, digits and '-'.
- Problems the config screens only warn about (SCSI IDs 0/7, no drive
  letters, an HDD image on the network) are returned as "warning".

ConfigStream::getSettingsReloadProxy() gives the resource the same reload
path as the config screens.
